      "description": "Watch Wrexham vs Burnley highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 8, 2026. The atmosphere was thick with anticipation on September 8, 2026 , as Wrexham hosted Burnley in a highly anticipated Championship fixture. Both sides took to the pitch looking to establish early dominance in a match that promised to be a fascinating tactical battle. First Half Breakthrough The contest began with a high-tempo physical struggle, leading to an early booking for Issa Kabore in the 14th minute. The deadlock was finally broken in the 26th minute when Zeki Amdouni clinical finish found the back of the net, following a well-crafted assist from Largie Ramazani . Wrexham faced further challenges shortly after the opening goal, as Max Cleworth was forced off the field and replaced by Zak Vyner in a defensive reshuffle just 30 minutes into the game. Clinical Finishing and Defensive Discipline The second half saw Wrexham introduce Callum O'Hare and Oliver Rathbone in an attempt to spark a comeback, but it was Burnley who struck next. In the 55th minute, Jacques Ekomie doubled the advantage with a composed strike, assisted by Issa Kabore . As the clock ticked down, the match grew increasingly feisty, resulting in yellow cards for Aaron Ramsey , Dominic Hyam , and Lucas Pires . Despite a late flurry of substitutions and six minutes of added time, Burnley remained resolute to secure all three points on the road."
